# KSV0125: Restrict container images to trusted registries
# Trivy does not recognize ghcr.io as trusted by default. We use ghcr.io for application images.
# Registry validation is enforced at deployment time via policy/OPA Gatekeeper.
KSV0125

# KSV020, KSV021: runAsUser/runAsGroup > 10000
# OpenShift restricted-v2 SCC assigns namespace-specific UID range (e.g. 1002750000-1002759999).
# Cannot hardcode in template; OpenShift injects at deploy time.
KSV020
KSV021

# KSV030, KSV104: seccompProfile
# OpenShift restricted SCC forbids seccomp: "seccomp may not be set".
KSV030
KSV104

# KSV0013: "Image tag ':latest' used" false-positive on templated image refs.
# The canonical parameterized templates enforce REGISTRY:IMAGE_TAG. The
# deployment pipeline sets IMAGE_TAG per build (PR number/test/prod), so
# runtime images are always tagged explicitly.
KSV0013
KSV-0013

# CVE-2025-10492: JasperReports Java deserialization issue.
#
# Severity: HIGH. Fixed upstream in JR 7.0.4, but JR 7.x currently breaks this
# codebase's legacy JRXML compilation path ("Unable to load report"), including
# OracleLegacyJasperTableReportServiceTest.
#
# Scope/risk in this service:
#   - We compile JRXML files bundled in src/main/resources only.
#   - We do not load attacker-controlled .jasper binaries.
#   - No user upload path feeds Jasper binary deserialization.
#
# Re-evaluate when Jasper 7.x supports our legacy templates without breaking
# report parity.
CVE-2025-10492

# CVE-2026-3260: Undertow Denial of Service via premature multipart/form-data
# parsing on GET requests.
#
# Severity: MEDIUM. Backend intentionally uses Undertow to align with nr-rept.
# The only fixed Undertow release currently available is 2.4.0.Beta1.
#
# Current mitigations:
#   - Request body limits are enforced upstream.
#   - /api surface is Cognito/JWT protected.
#   - Pod memory limits bound blast radius to pod restart.
#
# Re-evaluate when a stable Undertow fix lands in a non-beta release.
CVE-2026-3260
